# ========================================
# SIF 3.7 Certification Tests - Credentials
# ========================================
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in your actual credentials.
#
# These credentials are used by each test section's setup steps (01-create-domain,
# 02-create-solution, 03-get-admin-environment, 99-teardown) to create and delete
# the certification domain and solution. Section-specific infrastructure is managed
# using credentials derived from the solution (stored in Bruno vars by step 03).
#
# Credential Naming Pattern:
#   {currentEnv}-{role}SessionToken
#   {currentEnv}-{role}SharedSecret
#
# Where:
#   - currentEnv = value from your Bruno environment file (e.g., "cert")
#   - role = "admin" (the only role needed for domain/solution management)
#
# The admin credentials must have permission to create and delete
# domains and solutions on the target broker.

# ========================================
# Certification Environment (default)
# ========================================
# Admin credentials for domain/solution lifecycle
cert-adminSessionToken=<your-admin-session-token>
cert-adminSharedSecret=<your-admin-shared-secret>

# ========================================
# Solution-Admin Mode (runAsGlobalAdmin=false)
# ========================================
# When the environment sets `runAsGlobalAdmin: false`, the suite runs as a
# per-solution "solution admin" (the broker-services environment for a
# pre-provisioned domain+solution). In that mode:
#
#   - Tests tagged `globaladminonly` (create-domain, create-solution,
#     tag-definition creation, domain teardown) are SKIPPED. Run with:
#         bru run <section> --env <env> --exclude-tags globaladminonly
#   - The domain and solution must already exist (provisioned out of band).
#     Their identifiers are read from the static values below instead of being
#     created during the run.
#   - Section operational tests authenticate with the solution-admin
#     credentials below instead of the global admin credentials above.
#
# Solution-admin credentials = the broker-services environment's session token
# and shared secret for the pre-provisioned solution (copy from the admin
# console "Internal Broker Services" environment, or rotate and copy).
#
#   {currentEnv}-solutionAdminSessionToken / -solutionAdminSharedSecret
#   {currentEnv}-domainId  / {currentEnv}-solutionId  (pre-provisioned scope)
#
# Example for currentEnv=cert:
# cert-solutionAdminSessionToken=<broker-services-session-token>
# cert-solutionAdminSharedSecret=<broker-services-shared-secret>
# cert-domainId=<pre-provisioned-domain-id>
# cert-solutionId=<pre-provisioned-solution-id>
